- macro that generates other unit struct with &mut Graph and methods to solve stems

- With my graph system, a node could hold many curves. A user edit node could mutate the node that holds a ton of curves.
- could this be implemented without RwLock? Yes, if the nodes are kept in a HashMap

- The user could have a group of curves in the ECS. My graph watches that group which is just a list of curve indices. It can then produce flat version for GPU
all at once. It might involve adding some additional information like thickness and color. 
The point is that the shape of the graph is fixed. A new graph must be made if the situation changes.

- it is exetremely difficult or impossible to ensure a valid data structure at creation
    - instead, I can ensure a valid method 

- it does not make logical sense to bound a struct by some typenum trait
- itsead I could implement functions on the structs. So if I want to pull a rank 5 block, 
    it needs rank 4 blocks. 

- call a topological object without bounds a Block
- Shape is a Block with Block bounds. The bounds must have dimensionality equal to the cardinality of the bounded Block
- Flow is two Blocks connected in series

- For intersection of planes, there is two kinds of symbolic curve. The first is the MAYBE curve. The second is the existing curve of extrusion form.
- For intersection of NURBS surfaces, there is two cymbolic curves. The first is the Maybe curves. The second is a specific curve of two surface and starting point. Then there are discrete NURBS surface intersections.
- For plane-cylinder intersection, there is two symbolic curves. The first is MAYBE curve. The second is ellipse. Instead of finding the ellipse, it might be easier to just find the discrete starting points like how I will with NURBS intersections. But if I do find the ellipse, I can maybe go fast and more accurate evenly spaced points.

- The Shape can list curves, surfaces, and then curves again because curves can be made from intersection of surfaces.
   - No, specifying a curve after surfaces is not the same as the first curve specification. It is specifying MAYBE curves

- I can dispatch(1, 1, 1) with workgroup size of 1 and loop 1024 overlap results to set an index buffer and dispatch size for the next 
  overlap check for GPU only BVH. This one shot dispatch could be more than one if processing multiple intersection checks at once.
- The shape structure needs a way to specify semantic groups. This way, BVH can be more effecient without automatically building a group tree which 
  is expensive
- I can do all the form::Spline in one dispatch if I accept some loops ending early. This way, a shape could be one Hedge where every type of operation
 is present with a dispatch size x y z for each op in the buffer. With this setup, a 

